BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:🚧 Windrush line: Highbury & Islington to Clapham Junction\, New
  Cross and New Cross Gate\, including during Saturday Night Overground ser
 vice
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
UID:3984c623c9190478bb8c@tfl-closures
CATEGORIES:Part of the line closed
DESCRIPTION:🚧 Part of the line closed\n\nHighbury & Islington to Clapha
 m Junction\, New Cross and New Cross Gate\, including during Saturday Nigh
 t Overground service\nDates as listed by TfL: Saturday 28 November to Sund
 ay 29 November 2026\n\nTfL live status (Part Closure\, checked 27 November
  2026): WINDRUSH LINE: From 0100 Saturday 28 and all day Sunday 29 Novembe
 r\, including Friday and Saturday Night Overground\, no service between Hi
 ghbury & Islington and Battersea Park / Clapham Junction / New Cross / New
  Cross Gate. Use MILDMAY LINE services between Highbury & Islington\, Cano
 nbury and Dalston Kingsland. Replacement bus services operate.\nTfL live s
 tatus (Reduced Service\, checked 27 November 2026): WINDRUSH LINE: Saturda
 y 28 and Sunday 29 November\, a reduced service operates between New Cross
  Gate and Crystal Palace / West Croydon.\nTfL live status (Part Closure\, 
 checked 27 November 2026): WINDRUSH LINE: Sunday 29 November\, until 0800
 \, no service between Sydenham and West Croydon. Customers should use loca
 l buses or trams via any reasonable route. First Trains: New Cross Gate to
  West Croydon 0747\; West Croydon to New Cross Gate 0818. In addition\, SO
 UTHERN trains between London Bridge and Caterham will not call at Norwood 
 Junction at this time.\n\nSource: TfL planned track closures\, correct at 
 Monday 16 November 2026. https://tfl.gov.uk/api/document/plannedtrackclosu
 res.pdf?id=accc98cf-e761-47b3-a43b-3de08a097b8f&type=document\nPlans can c
 hange. Check before you travel: https://tfl.gov.uk/tube-dlr-overground/sta
 tus/\nPowered by TfL Open Data\nUnofficial calendar\, not produced or endo
 rsed by Transport for London.
