BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:🌙 Windrush line: New Cross Gate to Crystal Palace and West Croy
 don\, after 23:30
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261207T233000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261208T013000
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
UID:b909c6a44b0890d103b4@tfl-closures
CATEGORIES:Closure in the late evening or overnight only
DESCRIPTION:🌙 Closure in the late evening or overnight only\n\nNew Cros
 s Gate to Crystal Palace and West Croydon\, after 23:30\nDates as listed b
 y TfL: Monday 7 December to Thursday 10 December 2026\n\nTfL live status (
 Part Closure\, checked 27 November 2026): WINDRUSH LINE: Monday 7\, Tuesda
 y 8\, Wednesday 9 and Thursday 10 November\, after 2330 each evening\, no 
 service between New Cross Gate and West Croydon / Crystal Palace. Rail rep
 lacement buses will run as follows: The bus for Crystal Palace will depart
  London Bridge at 2358 calling at New Cross Gate\, Brockley\, Honor Oak Pa
 rk\, Forest Hill\, Sydenham\, Crystal Palace\, Gipsy Hill\, West Norwood\,
  Tulse Hill and Streatham Hill. The bus for East Croydon will depart Londo
 n Bridge at 0035 calling at New Cross Gate\, Brockley\, Honor Oak Park\, F
 orest Hill\, Sydenham\, Norwood Junction and East Croydon (Arr 01:27). One
  return bus from Crystal Palace departs at 2359\, calling at all stations 
 to London Bridge via New Cross Gate. Alternatively\, use local buses or tr
 ams via any reasonable route. The 2232 and 2247 trains from Highbury & Isl
 ington to West Croydon will both divert to Crystal Palace. The 2338 train 
 from Dalston Junction to New Cross Gate will not run\n\nSource: TfL planne
 d track closures\, correct at Monday 16 November 2026. https://tfl.gov.uk/
 api/document/plannedtrackclosures.pdf?id=accc98cf-e761-47b3-a43b-3de08a097
 b8f&type=document\nPlans can change. Check before you travel: https://tfl.
 gov.uk/tube-dlr-overground/status/\nPowered by TfL Open Data\nUnofficial c
 alendar\, not produced or endorsed by Transport for London.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
